          "mechanism": "Real estate is valued using capitalization rates tied to the 10-year rate, and properties are financed with long-term debt, so rising long rates directly lower property values and raise financing costs. Falling rates do the opposite and lift valuations. The sector is one of the most rate-sensitive in the market.",
          "buyAvoid": "Buy when the 10-year rate is falling. Avoid when the 10-year rate is rising sharply.",
