          "mechanism": "Most globally traded materials are priced in dollars, so a weaker dollar mechanically raises their prices and producer revenue, while a stronger dollar lowers them. Materials companies also earn foreign revenue that translates more favorably when the dollar is weak. This dual exposure makes Materials highly dollar-sensitive.",
