          "why": "Inventory levels at the US delivery hub reveal whether the WTI move is driven by genuine supply-demand tightness or by a storage buildup, so reading them alongside the price confirms the cause of the move. Falling inventories confirm tightness while rising inventories signal oversupply. This separates a real supply-demand move from a local storage effect.",
