          "meaning": "Individual investors are close to fully invested and hold almost no reserve. Buying power has been spent, so the marginal buyer needed to push prices higher is largely absent, and any forced selling has no cash cushion behind it. This condition has appeared near major peaks, most clearly in January 2000. It argues for reducing the aggressive sectors the crowd already owns and adding sectors whose earnings do not depend on rising asset prices.",
