          "mechanism": "The sector is high beta and depends on household willingness to spend, so it both leads market rebounds and suffers most when the bid fades. A large cash reserve is doubly favorable, because the same reserve that can buy stocks can also be spent on goods. Discretionary earnings and discretionary share prices respond to the same released reserve.",
