          "pairedMetric": "Net Charge-Off Rate, All Loans",
          "why": "The delinquency rate captures loans where payment has been missed while the charge-off rate captures losses banks have actually realized, so delinquencies lead and charge-offs confirm. Reading them together shows both the early warning and the eventual damage. This links the leading indicator to the lagging one.",
          "sharpens": "When delinquencies are rising AND charge-offs are still low, distress is building but losses have not yet crystallized, giving an early signal to rotate from Financials and cyclicals toward defensives. When both are elevated, the deterioration has fully arrived and the defensive rotation is confirmed."
