          "sharpens": "When unemployment is rising AND delinquencies are climbing, the cash-flow squeeze on borrowers is confirmed by its underlying cause, which strengthens the case for defensives. When unemployment is low AND delinquencies are stable, borrowers can service debt from income, which supports cyclical leadership."
