          "pairedMetric": "High-Yield Credit Spread",
          "why": "The stress index is a broad composite of many series, while the high-yield spread is the sharpest single read on default risk in the riskiest borrowers, so reading them together confirms whether rising stress is being driven by credit fear. Ziegel notes that when liquidity dries up market risk becomes credit risk, so the two move together in a genuine crisis. This combines a system-wide composite with a focused credit read.",
          "sharpens": "When the index is calm AND the high-yield spread is narrow, both broad and credit-specific stress are low, which supports Financials and cyclicals. When the index is rising AND the spread is widening, stress and credit fear are reinforcing each other, which confirms a turn toward crisis and argues for a defensive rotation."
